1
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:02,980
Most people learning Gen

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,940
AI stop at prompting.

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,460
But it's a full stack,

4
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,073
from tokens to agents,

5
00:00:08,093 --> 00:00:10,420
and the last eight are where the jobs are.

6
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:13,320
Here are the twenty you actually need.

7
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,280
Hi, I'm Chris.

8
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,680
I've spent over 10 years

9
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:17,640
in data engineering

10
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:20,520
and interviewed more than 200 engineers.

11
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:22,280
Now I run Stackle, where I teach

12
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,780
the skills that actually get you hired.

13
00:00:25,237 --> 00:00:27,084
One: tokens.

14
00:00:27,104 --> 00:00:28,817
Models read text in small pieces

15
00:00:28,837 --> 00:00:31,617
called tokens, and you pay per token.

16
00:00:31,637 --> 00:00:33,217
Two: embeddings.

17
00:00:33,237 --> 00:00:34,977
Text becomes a list of numbers,

18
00:00:34,997 --> 00:00:37,457
so similar meanings sit close together.

19
00:00:37,477 --> 00:00:39,137
Three: attention.

20
00:00:39,157 --> 00:00:40,977
Every token looks at every other

21
00:00:40,997 --> 00:00:43,057
token to work out what it means.

22
00:00:43,077 --> 00:00:45,164
Four: large language models.

23
00:00:45,184 --> 00:00:46,577
They predict the next token,

24
00:00:46,597 --> 00:00:48,097
one at a time.

25
00:00:48,117 --> 00:00:49,804
Five: the context window.

26
00:00:49,824 --> 00:00:52,337
How much text the model can see at once.

27
00:00:52,357 --> 00:00:53,937
Six: temperature.

28
00:00:53,957 --> 00:00:55,937
Low is focused and repeatable.

29
00:00:55,957 --> 00:00:57,617
High is more varied.

30
00:00:57,637 --> 00:00:59,057
Seven: prompting.

31
00:00:59,077 --> 00:01:00,097
Clear instructions,

32
00:01:00,117 --> 00:01:03,270
examples and a format give better answers.

33
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:04,417
Eight: few-shot.

34
00:01:04,437 --> 00:01:06,070
Show a few examples in the prompt,

35
00:01:06,090 --> 00:01:07,937
and the model follows the pattern.

36
00:01:07,957 --> 00:01:09,777
Nine: hallucinations.

37
00:01:09,797 --> 00:01:11,297
Answers that sound confident,

38
00:01:11,317 --> 00:01:12,417
but are made up.

39
00:01:12,437 --> 00:01:13,937
Ten: fine-tuning.

40
00:01:13,957 --> 00:01:15,537
Train a model further on your own

41
00:01:15,557 --> 00:01:17,697
examples to change how it behaves.

42
00:01:17,717 --> 00:01:19,937
Eleven: R L H F.

43
00:01:19,957 --> 00:01:21,190
People rank the answers,

44
00:01:21,210 --> 00:01:23,137
and the model learns what they prefer.

45
00:01:23,157 --> 00:01:24,737
Twelve: multimodal.

46
00:01:24,757 --> 00:01:26,497
One model that understands text,

47
00:01:26,517 --> 00:01:28,057
images and audio.

48
00:01:28,077 --> 00:01:29,297
Now the last eight.

49
00:01:29,317 --> 00:01:30,977
This is where the jobs are.

50
00:01:30,997 --> 00:01:33,057
Thirteen: vector databases.

51
00:01:33,077 --> 00:01:34,044
They store embeddings,

52
00:01:34,064 --> 00:01:36,257
and find the closest matches fast.

53
00:01:36,277 --> 00:01:37,697
Fourteen: chunking.

54
00:01:37,717 --> 00:01:39,137
Split long documents into

55
00:01:39,157 --> 00:01:40,817
small pieces you can search.

56
00:01:40,837 --> 00:01:42,257
Fifteen: RAG.

57
00:01:42,277 --> 00:01:44,017
Retrieve the right chunks first,

58
00:01:44,037 --> 00:01:46,337
then answer from them, with sources.

59
00:01:46,357 --> 00:01:47,910
Sixteen: tool calling.

60
00:01:47,930 --> 00:01:49,257
The model asks your code

61
00:01:49,277 --> 00:01:50,177
to run a function,

62
00:01:50,197 --> 00:01:51,537
like a database query.

63
00:01:51,557 --> 00:01:53,030
Seventeen: agents.

64
00:01:53,050 --> 00:01:54,817
A model in a loop that plans,

65
00:01:54,837 --> 00:01:57,057
uses tools and checks its own work.

66
00:01:57,077 --> 00:01:58,604
Eighteen: M C P.

67
00:01:58,624 --> 00:02:00,137
An open standard for plugging

68
00:02:00,157 --> 00:02:02,177
tools and data into AI apps.

69
00:02:02,197 --> 00:02:03,697
Nineteen: evals.

70
00:02:03,717 --> 00:02:05,137
Tests that score the answers,

71
00:02:05,157 --> 00:02:07,377
so you know a change made things better.

72
00:02:07,397 --> 00:02:08,897
Twenty: guardrails.

73
00:02:08,917 --> 00:02:11,030
Checks on what goes in and what comes out,

74
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:12,737
so the system stays safe.

75
00:02:12,757 --> 00:02:15,457
Tokens to agents: that's the full stack.

76
